      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-52",
        "notes": "Checked every step 1.1,1.2,2.1,3.1,4.1 against explicit matrices, units, bump supplier and complete current gauge-current proof. Smooth compact variations on U give the real-component Euler equation without extending fields. Adjoint derivative cancels gauge terms in the current divergence. Maxwell variation gives partial F=-mu0*j, matching Gauss/Ampere signs for F_0i=-E_i/c. q=0 and psi=0 require no division; current components carry A*m^-2 with j0=c*rho. Free correspondence uses AC_omega; the local variational argument adds no choice or empirical premise."
