      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-52",
        "notes": "Checked all seven steps and full Coulomb/finite-mode supplier proofs. Scalar source sign gives +phi*(div pi+rho) in H and pi=-epsilon0*E. Neutrality removes Fourier zero mode; L^3 converts normalized torus measure; rapid decay uniformly on compact time intervals supports smooth solver and positive energy. Finite orthonormal mode substitution gives kinetic term with hbar units, real canonical variables give complex brackets, invertible M for hbar>0 and reduced bracket -i/hbar. N>=1 excludes empty truncation. Electron-only neutrality forces psi=0; finite-mode kinematics are explicitly separate, with no CAR or PDE invariance claim. Conditional upstream statuses remain recorded."
