      "finite_smoke": [],
      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-52",
        "notes": "Checked all three steps and exact bump/quotient suppliers. kappa>0 keeps the support away from the apex; the inner ball gives positive bump norm. Auxiliary g*(1,0,0,0) has norm -1 and fails subsidiary condition on positive measure. On Omega, |n1|<=1/3 gives projected e1 norm squared >=8/9, permitting positive normalization. It uses only the positive-space part of photon-properties, not its open continuity clause. Hypothetical comparison makes no measurement or negative Born-probability claim."
