        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-52",
        "notes": "Checked both steps and current Gauss/Coulomb suppliers. L>0, q=-e<0 and nonzero constant spinor give Q<0; smooth periodic divergence integrates to zero by opposite-face cancellation, contradicting Gauss. The argument assumes a hypothetical Gauss-satisfying configuration and does not assume the spinor solves Dirac dynamics. Zero charge is the separate neutral branch; boundaries, punctures or exterior flux change hypotheses. No empirical data, statistical inference or observed charged cell asserted."
